  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_channel_statistics(images: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Per-Channel Mean and Std** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_channel_statistics(images: list) -> dict:\n    arr = np.array(images, dtype=float)\n    return {'channel_means': np.round(np.mean(arr, axis=(0, 2, 3)), 4).tolist(), 'channel_stds': np.round(np.std(arr, axis=(0, 2, 3)), 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
